From: swouapiy <swouapiy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Filenames are UTF-8

The cards' names are UTF-8 and the handheld has no locales: nl_langinfo() says ASCII,
and every name with an accent failed for SFTP 4 and later clients (WinSCP, for one).

Upstream: not applicable (Banana-specific)

---
--- a/sftpserver.c
+++ b/sftpserver.c
@@ -456,7 +456,9 @@
 
   /* We need I18N support for filename encoding */
   setlocale(LC_CTYPE, "");
-  local_encoding = nl_langinfo(CODESET);
+  /* Banana: the cards' names are UTF-8 (exFAT, iocharset=utf8) and the handheld has no locales, where
+   * nl_langinfo() says ASCII and every name with an accent failed for SFTP 4 and later clients */
+  local_encoding = "UTF-8";
 
   while((n = getopt_long(argc, argv, "hVdD:r:u:H:L:b46R", options, 0)) >= 0) {
     switch(n) {
